A1. This goes around the world every day. ~ SKY
A4. A good thing to take on a motor trip. ~ SPARE
A8. This goes for fare. ~ CAB
A11. This is a row. ~ TIER
A13. A collection of sayings. ~ ANA
A14. This kind of thing lacks color. ~ PALE
A15. You'll get credit for this. ~ ASSET
A17. Anything is pretty smooth this way. ~ OILED
A18. Part of the verb to be. ~ IS
A19. What the big guns were doing in 1918. ~ BOOMING
A22. In what direction is Florida from Kansas City. (Abbr.) ~ SE
A24. This is charming and attractive—and a girl's name. ~ GRACE
A26. A Grecian deity. ~ PAN
A28. What the doughboy did after the cook made a mess of things. ~ ATE
A29. Where some people go—on the water wagon. ~ SPA
A31. This is a well-known sparking place. ~ SEDAN
A32. Man-of-War's home sweet home. ~ STALL
A34. What a real sheik is. ~ ARAB
A35. This looks and acts like a donkey. ~ ASS
A37. If you have brains you may get this. ~ IDEA
A38. A yeggman's sweetie. ~ MOLL
A40. This goes with a horse's neck. ~ MANE
A43. What the barber is doing while you're waiting for a haircut. ~ BOBBING
A46. This is very deep stuff. ~ SEA
A48. When you meet these, you're out money. ~ BILLS
A49. This is always against you. ~ FOE
A51. Feminine name. ~ ANNA
A53. A well-known humorist. ~ NYE
A54. Pertaining to wings, winglike. ~ ALAR
A55. This has eyes—but sees not. ~ POTATO
A56. This is a pretty howdy-do in the army. ~ SALUTE

D1. If society won't take you up—this will. ~ STAIR
D2. This is pressing. ~ KISS
D3. A true diplomat rarely ever says this. ~ YES
D5. A silent pardner. ~ PA
D6. What the cup-that-cheers does. ~ ANIMATES
D7. The crossword sun-deity. ~ RA
D8. This man will move next March. ~ CAL
D9. Prohibitionists think it's a crime to drink these. ~ ALES
D10. To moisten. ~ BEDEW
D12. The boy in gray who refused to work for the government. (Abbr.) ~ REB
D14. This is noted for its greed. ~ PIG
D16. This is a matter of dress. ~ TOG
D17. This is singular. ~ ONE
D20. A day breeze on Lake Garda. (This is tough, so we'll give you the middle letter—R.) ~ ORA
D21. A winter cap. ~ ICE
D23. Spell the word up or down—it's a woman just the same. ~ MADAM
D25. This is used in digging up the dirt. ~ SPADE
D26. By means of. ~ PER
D27. Wealthy, luxurious man from the East. ~ NABOB
D29. What the busy little bees give you. ~ STING
D30. This is put down in Canada. ~ ALE
D31. To sink under pressure. ~ SAG
D33. You'll never get ahead if you do this. ~ LAG
D35. What is the white-headed boy? ~ ALBINO
D36. There's a mile between the first and last letter of this word. ~ SMILES
D39. A high-ball. ~ LOB
D41. What a young man who writes for money hopes to get. (Abbr.) ~ ANS
D42. Where the Battle Cry of Freedom is sung. ~ RENO
D44. Who was that Nellie who went around the world in less than eighty days? ~ BLY
D45. A very good butter. ~ GOAT
D46. This is sweet—and a bit thick. ~ SAP
D47. This is notably a hard worker. ~ ANT
D49. A war-time epidemic. (Abbr.) ~ FLU
D50. Sooner than. ~ ERE
D52. American Association. (Abbr.) ~ AA
D54. The man in the brown derby. ~ AL


